  "challenge": "ESCALATE is unnecessary because AR-004 is already dispositive: subtotal $21,040.00 + tax $1,472.80 = $22,512.80, yet the stated total is $22,562.80—an unambiguous $50 overcharge with no additional_charges line to explain it. That is a machine-verifiable internal inconsistency; the invoice should be rejected for correction and resubmission, not parked for a human to re-add the same figures. PO-001’s over-threshold approval and the three IN-003 stock overs (22/15, 18/10, 9/5) only matter on a mathematically valid total—until then they are moot. Vendor record confirms Atlas Industrial Supply is active since 2019 with matching Net 60 terms, and get_prior_invoice found no prior INV-1013, so there is no duplicate or identity question to reconcile; PR-003 dual prices sit at/under reference ($250/$500/$750) and are labeled volume discount. Send it back.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["AR-004", "PO-001", "IN-003"]
